('127.152.d.2.A',3,'Independent critical thinking means evaluating a plan:','["By luck", "By copying others", "By guessing", "On your own using evidence"]'::jsonb,3,'Critical.','original'),
('127.152.d.2.A',4,'A team evaluating design options critically should share:','["Reasons and evidence", "Only votes", "Only jokes", "Only opinions"]'::jsonb,0,'Team analysis.','original'),
('127.152.d.2.B',3,'To solve a tight-site problem creatively, an architect might first:','["Ignore the site", "Sketch several layout options", "Quit", "Pick one at once"]'::jsonb,1,'Creative solutions.','original'),
('127.152.d.2.B',4,'A site with a steep slope can be an opportunity to design:','["A floating roof", "A flat shoebox only", "Stepped levels that follow the land", "No building"]'::jsonb,2,'Innovate.','original'),
('127.152.d.2.C',3,'A weighted decision matrix with scores for cost, function, and appearance helps the team:','["Avoid deciding", "Delay", "Hide scores", "Choose among options fairly"]'::jsonb,3,'Decision-making.','original'),
('127.152.d.2.C',4,'In a weighted matrix, a criterion with a higher weight:','["Has more influence on the final score", "Is removed", "Has less influence", "Is ignored"]'::jsonb,0,'Weighting.','original'),
('127.152.d.2.D',3,'To improve a product by a problem-solving strategy, a team first:','["Hides it", "Names the problem clearly", "Paints it", "Prints it"]'::jsonb,1,'Strategy.','original'),
('127.152.d.2.D',4,'After testing a prototype, the team uses the results to:','["Hide the test", "Throw it away", "Refine the design", "Skip the next step"]'::jsonb,2,'Iterate.','original'),
('127.152.d.2.E',3,'Critical-thinking strategies for evaluating a product include asking:','["Is it blue?", "Is it loud?", "Is it pretty?", "Does it meet the stated needs?"]'::jsonb,3,'Evaluate.','original'),
('127.152.d.2.E',4,'When analyzing why a prototype failed, the team should look for:','["The root cause", "A new color", "A bigger budget", "Someone to blame"]'::jsonb,0,'Root cause.','original'),
('127.152.d.2.F',3,'Technical research for a design decision may use:','["Social posts", "Manufacturer data and codes", "Guesswork", "Gossip"]'::jsonb,1,'Research.','original'),
('127.152.d.2.F',4,'Which source is most reliable for a material''s fire rating?','["A rumor", "A random comment", "The manufacturer''s tested data sheet", "A stranger''s opinion"]'::jsonb,2,'Reliable sources.','original'),
('127.152.d.3.A',3,'Workplace safety rules in a design studio include keeping walkways:','["Dark", "Wet", "Blocked", "Clear of cords and boxes"]'::jsonb,3,'Studio safety.','original'),
('127.152.d.3.A',4,'Ergonomic safety at a drafting workstation includes adjusting:','["Chair height and monitor position", "Room number", "Pencil brand", "Paper color"]'::jsonb,0,'Ergonomics.','original'),
('127.152.d.3.B',3,'Hazardous materials such as spray adhesive are disposed of:','["In any trash can", "According to safety data sheet instructions", "Down the drain", "Outside"]'::jsonb,1,'Disposal.','original'),
('127.152.d.3.B',4,'Before using a new chemical in the model shop, check the:','["Price tag", "Brand", "Safety data sheet", "Color"]'::jsonb,2,'Hazards.','original'),
('127.152.d.3.C',3,'A laser cutter must be used with:','["Open flame", "Wet floors", "No guard", "Ventilation and supervision"]'::jsonb,3,'Equipment safety.','original'),
('127.152.d.3.C',4,'Before operating any shop tool, a student should receive:','["Training and permission", "A day off", "A prize", "A snack"]'::jsonb,0,'Training first.','original'),
('127.152.d.4.A',3,'A positive work ethic in an architecture office means meeting:','["Strangers", "Deadlines", "Birds", "Nobody"]'::jsonb,1,'Work ethic.','original'),
('127.152.d.4.A',4,'Taking responsibility for a mistake in a drawing means:','["Blaming others", "Hiding it", "Admitting it and fixing it", "Deleting it"]'::jsonb,2,'Accountability.','original'),
('127.152.d.4.B',3,'Ethical reasoning in architecture means considering the effect on:','["Only speed", "Only profit", "Only fame", "Public safety and the client"]'::jsonb,3,'Ethical reasoning.','original'),
('127.152.d.4.B',4,'If a client asks you to leave out a required fire exit, you should:','["Decline and explain the code", "Remove it", "Hide it", "Ignore the code"]'::jsonb,0,'Ethics.','original'),
('127.152.d.4.C',3,'Ethical practice as defined by the architectural industry includes protecting the:','["Paint stock", "Health, safety, and welfare of the public", "Architect''s fame", "Competition"]'::jsonb,1,'Professional ethics.','original'),
('127.152.d.4.C',4,'Plagiarism in design means:','["Citing sources", "Sketching", "Passing off someone else''s work as your own", "Giving credit"]'::jsonb,2,'Ethics.','original'),
('127.152.d.4.D',3,'Complying with rules consistently includes following the:','["Code on some projects", "Code never", "Code when watched", "Building code on every project"]'::jsonb,3,'Compliance.','original'),
('127.152.d.4.D',4,'A design that does not meet the required setback may need to be:','["Revised before approval", "Painted", "Hidden", "Built anyway"]'::jsonb,0,'Compliance.','original'),
('127.152.d.5.A',3,'In a supervised practicum with an architect, a student documents:','["Jokes", "Tasks, hours, and skills learned", "Songs", "Gossip"]'::jsonb,1,'Documentation.','original'),
('127.152.d.5.A',4,'A practicum student''s supervisor evaluates progress using:','["Weather", "Luck", "Observations and the student''s documentation", "Rumors"]'::jsonb,2,'Evaluation.','original'),
('127.152.d.5.B',3,'Advanced technical knowledge may include understanding:','["Cooking", "Music", "Hair care", "Structural systems and building envelope"]'::jsonb,3,'Technical.','original'),
('127.152.d.5.B',4,'The building envelope refers to the building''s:','["Exterior shell separating inside from outside", "Parking", "Furniture", "Floor plan"]'::jsonb,0,'Envelope.','original'),
('127.152.d.5.C',3,'Reading a set of construction documents requires understanding:','["Songs", "Symbols, scales, and notes", "Recipes", "Poems"]'::jsonb,1,'Reading drawings.','original'),
('127.152.d.5.C',4,'A detail callout on a plan refers the reader to:','["The budget", "The weather", "A more detailed drawing elsewhere", "The owner"]'::jsonb,2,'Callouts.','original'),
('127.152.d.5.D',3,'Designing a multimedia rendering product starts with:','["Buying paper", "Choosing a font", "Hiding data", "Understanding the message and audience"]'::jsonb,3,'Design process.','original'),
('127.152.d.5.D',4,'A good rendering design emphasizes the:','["Key features of the building", "Backgrounds only", "Colors only", "Credits"]'::jsonb,0,'Focus.','original'),
('127.152.d.5.E',3,'Producing a rendering uses software that applies:','["Paint", "Materials, lighting, and camera views", "Fabric", "Wood"]'::jsonb,1,'Production.','original'),
('127.152.d.5.E',4,'Before sharing a final rendering, the student should check it for:','["Parking", "Smells", "Accuracy and quality", "Time of day"]'::jsonb,2,'Quality.','original'),
('127.152.d.5.F',3,'Evaluating strengths and weaknesses in technical skill helps the student:','["Blame others", "Quit", "Hide errors", "Plan improvement"]'::jsonb,3,'Self-evaluation.','original'),
('127.152.d.5.F',4,'A student strong at sketching but slower at CAD should:','["Practice CAD with timed exercises", "Stop sketching", "Quit", "Avoid CAD"]'::jsonb,0,'Target weakness.','original'),
('127.152.d.5.G',3,'Representative work samples in an architectural practicum include:','["Menus", "Plans, sketches, and renderings", "Songs", "Gossip"]'::jsonb,1,'Samples.','original'),
('127.152.d.5.G',4,'A portfolio piece should be selected because it shows:','["Nothing", "Random scribbles", "Your best, representative skill", "The worst work"]'::jsonb,2,'Selection.','original'),
('127.150.d.5.O',5,'A student''s wall passes level checks but fails on joint consistency. The best self-evaluation response is to:','["Blame the mortar", "Hide the result", "Stop laying brick", "Record the weakness and practice uniform joints"]'::jsonb,3,'Honest self-evaluation drives improvement.','original'),
('127.151.d.10.A',5,'Under workplace rights in an architecture firm, an intern who sees an unsafe studio condition should:','["Report it to a supervisor", "Fix wiring alone", "Leave quietly", "Ignore it"]'::jsonb,0,'Employees may report hazards.','original'),
('127.151.d.10.G',5,'Which resume entry best fits an architectural design student?','["Likes movies", "Built a scale model and presented it to a panel", "Enjoys naps", "Owns a car"]'::jsonb,1,'Relevant, specific experience.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
join public.teks_items i on i.code = v.code and i.is_standard
join public.teks_documents d on d.id = i.document_id and d.subject = 'Career Development' and d.language = 'en'
on conflict (fingerprint) do nothing;
